{
    "_about":  [
                   "The target languages: canonical code, English name, endonym, script and text direction.",
                   "",
                   "51 rows, and the only list of languages in the tree. What a given model can actually do",
                   "with them is not here: per model support is a set of references into these codes, each",
                   "carrying the source it was read from, in model-languages.json. The flag or code badge a",
                   "row is drawn with is a second explicit table, language-assets.json, so nothing anywhere",
                   "derives artwork from a code.",
                   "",
                   "\u0027script\u0027 is the ISO 15924 code for the writing system, which is why zh-CN and zh-TW are",
                   "Hans and Hant rather than one Chinese.",
                   "",
                   "\u0027dir\u0027 is rtl for Arabic, Persian, Hebrew and Urdu. Nothing in the engine reorders text",
                   "for them; it is carried so a host can set dir= on its output.",
                   "",
                   "\u0027alias\u0027 exists for codes that are commonly written wrong. Ukrainian is uk in ISO 639-1;",
                   "ua is the country code, and i18n tooling that expects uk will not find a ua file."
               ],
